// Min-Mozhi example (Tamil flavor — same grammar, only the keywords change): parameterized shift register.
// `<<` shifts in zeros from the right and GROWS by the shift amount, so
// `trunc` drops the bit that falls off the top. `|` merges in the new low
// bit every clock edge. `din` is 1 bit and `sr` is WIDTH bits — widths
// never match implicitly, so `extend(din, WIDTH)` makes the resize visible.

தொகுதி ShiftRegister(WIDTH: int = 8) {
  துடிப்பு clk
  மீட்டமை rst

  உள்ளீடு  din:  bit
  வெளியீடு dout: bits[WIDTH]

  பதிவேடு sr: bits[WIDTH] = 0

  போது ஏற்றம்(clk) {
    sr <- trunc(sr << 1, WIDTH) | extend(din, WIDTH)
  }

  dout = sr
}
